 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Not necessarily. Cold actually helps with congested and irritated muscles. The problem is stopping off wind can be dangerous. Cover them with a thick blanket then. Put your hands in your pockets or a good pair of gloves. The key is keeping your fingers and toes warm, so your body can stay warm too. That's the sensible option. Snow takes ages to melt, and buses are designed to handle it. Yes, studded or snow tired are worth it. They grip the road in the snow and ice much better than summer tyres.",
